<ProductLayout title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} ogImage="/images/uploads/2025/09/1-1024x1024.jpg" gallery={gallery} category={category} descriptionHtml={`<p>Cost-effective <a href="/product/" title="Feed additives">feed</a>-grade amino acid source: <strong>L-Lysine Sulphate 70%</strong> (≥55% available lysine). Widely applied in poultry, swine, and aquaculture nutrition to optimize growth and feed efficiency. Samples available, bulk packaging customizable.</p><h2>1. Product Names &amp; Synonyms</h2><ul><li>Official name: <strong>L-Lysine Sulphate 70% (Feed Grade)</strong></li><li>Synonyms: L-lysine sulphate, lysine sulphate (feed grade), 70% lysine sulphate, lysine sulphate granules</li><li>CAS No.: <strong>60343-69-3</strong></li><li>Molecular Formula: <strong>C₆H₁₆N₂O₆S</strong></li><li>Common abbreviation: <strong>L-Lysine Sulphate 70%</strong></li></ul><hr/><h2>2. Technical Specifications &amp; Properties</h2><p><strong>Guaranteed Analysis</strong></p><ul><li>L-lysine sulphate (as salt): ~70%</li><li>Available L-lysine (free base): ≥55%</li><li>Other amino acids: ≥10% (fermentation by-products)</li><li>Moisture: ≤3.0%</li><li>Ash: ≤4.0%</li><li>pH (1% solution): 3.0–6.5 (typical ≈3.5)</li><li>Sulphate content: ≤15%</li><li>Heavy metals: ≤0.003%</li><li>Shelf life: 24 months (unopened, dry conditions at ambient temperature)</li></ul><p><strong>Physical Properties</strong></p><ul><li>Appearance: light brown to yellowish free-flowing powder or granules</li><li>Solubility: easily soluble in water, insoluble in oil</li><li>Bulk density: 600–650 kg/m³ (≈0.60–0.65 g/cm³)</li><li>Particle size: ≥90% pass 1.55–1.7 mm sieve</li></ul><p><strong>Chemical Properties</strong></p><ul><li>Molecular weight: ~244.26 g/mol</li><li>Stability: stable under dry, cool, and light-protected conditions</li><li>Reactivity: Avoid prolonged high-temperature processing to reduce Maillard reactions</li></ul><hr/><h2>4. Application &amp; Usage</h2><p><strong>Calculation Formula</strong><br/>Required lysine (g/kg) ÷ Available lysine fraction (0.55) = Dosage of L-Lysine Sulphate (g/kg feed).</p><p><strong>Dosage Examples</strong></p><ul><li>To supply 1.0 g/kg lysine → add <strong>1.82 g/kg (1.82 kg/ton)</strong> L-Lysine Sulphate</li><li>To supply 1.5 g/kg lysine → add <strong>2.73 g/kg (2.73 kg/ton)</strong></li><li>To supply 2.0 g/kg lysine → add <strong>3.64 g/kg (3.64 kg/ton)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Species Applications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Swine (30–60 kg grower pigs):</strong> Target SID lysine ≈0.94% (9.4 g/kg). If basal feed provides 7.5 g/kg, supplement 1.9 g/kg → add <strong>3.45 kg/ton</strong>.</li><li><strong>Broilers:</strong> Target ≈1.0% lysine. If basal feed has 8.5 g/kg, supplement 1.6 g/kg → add <strong>2.91 kg/ton</strong>.</li><li><strong>Layers / Aquaculture:</strong> Dosage depends on growth stage; calculate with a formula based on NRC or company nutrition standards.</li><li><strong>Ruminants:</strong> Not effective unless rumen-protected, since unprotected lysine is degraded in the rumen.</li></ul><p><strong>Best Practices</strong></p><ul><li>Pre-mix in small batches before blending into the final feed.</li><li>Monitor heat treatment (pelleting) to avoid lysine loss.</li><li>Use appropriate PPE (mask, goggles) to prevent dust exposure.</li></ul><hr/><h2>5. Packaging &amp; Storage</h2><ul><li>Packaging: 25 kg carton drums, kraft bags with PE liner, or jumbo bags (500–1000 kg).</li><li>Storage: keep sealed, dry, at ambient temperature, away from heat, moisture, and direct sunlight.</li><li>Shelf life: 24 months unopened under recommended storage.</li><li>Safety: dust may cause irritation; handle with ventilation and protective equipment.</li></ul><hr/><h2>6. Comparison with L-Lysine HCl</h2><ul><li><strong>Purity vs dosage</strong>: L-Lysine HCl contains 98.5% salt (~78% lysine), requires a lower inclusion rate but is more expensive.</li><li><strong>Economics</strong>: L-Lysine Sulphate provides similar nutritional value at a lower cost per unit of usable lysine.</li><li><strong>Practicality</strong>: Both are highly bioavailable; choice depends on feed mill economics and formulation precision.</li></ul><hr/><h2>7. Quality Control (Buyer Checklist)</h2><ul><li>Test items: lysine content, moisture, ash, particle size, heavy metals, microbiology.</li><li>Methods: HPLC for amino acid content, ICP-MS for heavy metals, and standard ISO/GB for microbes.</li><li>Documents: COA, SDS, heavy metal &amp; microbiological reports provided with shipment.</li></ul><hr/><h2>9. Specification Table</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Product Name</td><td>L-Lysine Sulphate 70% (Feed Grade)</td></tr><tr><td>CAS No.</td><td>60343-69-3</td></tr><tr><td>Molecular Formula</td><td>C₆H₁₆N₂O₆S</td></tr><tr><td>Molecular Weight</td><td>244.26 g/mol</td></tr><tr><td>Available Lysine</td><td>≥55%</td></tr><tr><td>L-Lysine Sulphate</td><td>~70%</td></tr><tr><td>Moisture</td><td>≤3.0%</td></tr><tr><td>Ash</td><td>≤4.0%</td></tr><tr><td>pH (1% solution)</td><td>3.0–6.5</td></tr><tr><td>Bulk Density</td><td>600–650 kg/m³</td></tr><tr><td>Particle Size</td><td>≥90% through 1.55–1.7 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Appearance</td><td>Light brown/yellowish powder or granules</td></tr><tr><td>Packaging</td><td>25 kg drums or jumbo bags</td></tr><tr><td>Shelf Life</td><td>24 months unopened</td></tr></tbody></table>`} />
